ifies an existing crisis over the court's credibility and internal governance just as it has expanded its political role.\n\nMeanwhile, Lula is working to normalise relations with Washington. Donald Trump said he 'gets along very well' with the Brazilian president and would 'love' to meet him, while Lula expressed a desire for 'equal treatment' from the United States. The Brazilian government is preparing for a bilateral meeting expected between March 15-20, though Lula was not invited to Trump's gathering of Latin American allies. Brazil still condemned US-Israeli attacks on Iran, demonstrating its continued multi-alignment strategy even as it seeks better ties with Washington.\"}",
